0..81 Comment "//! A doubly recursive function of twelve levels answers true without allocating."
82..85 Comment "//!"
86..167 Comment "//! Boespflug, Dénès and Grégoire make 2^27 trivial calls, so the run measures"
168..243 Comment "//! calls without garbage collection. Their native code gained most on that"
244..257 Comment "//! workload."
258..261 Comment "//!"
262..337 Comment "//! Each level calls the level below twice and answers a constant. The path"
338..376 Comment "//! reads the answer at twelve levels."
377..380 Comment "//!"
381..460 Comment "//! - cites: [Boespflug-2011-full_reduction_at_full_throttle], § 4, RecNoAlloc"
461..499 Comment "//! - see: #2282 — the benchmark set"
